# Rules the spec declares that no Go source cites — the ratchet half of
# scripts/rule-citations.sh. One rule per line: the id, then a reason.
#
# THE LIST MAY ONLY SHRINK. Cite a rule and its line goes; the script fails on a
# listed rule that has since been cited, so the list cannot rot into a permanent
# exemption that silences the "uncited and unlisted" failure.
#
# Two shapes of reason, and no third:
#
#   another layer's — the rule governs something this library never does. It
#                     stands as long as that holds, and a line moves out of this
#                     shape only when the library takes the rule on.
#   sweep sd-924c13 — this library enforces the rule and no comment says so. The
#                     line names where the citation belongs, so the sweep adds
#                     it at the enforcing site rather than anywhere convenient.
#
# A reason that says only "not yet" says nothing: it neither justifies the
# exemption nor names what removes it.

# Access — accounts, targets, and the letters they hold. Grants are server
# configuration resolved before a call reaches the library, which sees only the
# constraints it is handed (Constraints, contribution.go).
R-AGRANT      another layer's: grants and accounts are the server's configuration
R-ABRANCH     another layer's: per-branch rights are checked before the library is called
R-ATABLE      another layer's: rights over $branches are the server's to check
R-AUNIVERSE   another layer's: the privileged $universe read is the server's to grant

# ADT rules — the definition of valid, enforced in the root package.
V-TYPE        sweep sd-924c13: type vocabulary, node_taxonomy.go + edge_taxonomy.go
V-REF         sweep sd-924c13: every edge reference resolves, verify.go closure walk
V-ROOT        sweep sd-924c13: initial claim or contributor edge, claim.go
V-CONTENT     sweep sd-924c13: size + encoding, inline xor hash, verify.go ruleContent
V-ID          sweep sd-924c13: id over stored bytes, verify.go verifyID
V-SIG         sweep sd-924c13: signature under the signer's pubkey, verify.go ruleSignature
V-MONO        sweep sd-924c13: created_at at or after every reference's, verify.go
V-HEIGHT      sweep sd-924c13: height = 1 + max(refs), verify.go verifyHeight
V-HASH        sweep sd-924c13: multihash framing, id.go + verify_content.go
V-ALIAS       sweep sd-924c13: alias forms, field_taxonomy.go + encoding_taxonomy.go
V-DIFF        sweep sd-924c13: overlay to a base claim, node.go computeDiffFields
V-DIFFEDGE    sweep sd-924c13: edge inheritance by name, claim_assemble.go
V-REL         sweep sd-924c13: relation_direction on relation/*, edge.go
V-PROV        sweep sd-924c13: derivation/entity/relation nodes carry a reference, verify.go

# Contribution rules — the six-step procedure. Steps 1, 4 (sealing), 5, and 6
# are the write path in adapter/sequencer; the rest are the contribution itself.
R-C1BASE      sweep sd-924c13: base (k, t) at open, adapter/sequencer
R-C2DATE      sweep sd-924c13: no claim dated after the base time, adapter/sequencer
R-C2TYPE      sweep sd-924c13: reserved types, contribution.go reservedTypes
R-C3CLOSE     sweep sd-924c13: closing over references, contribution.go
R-C3LIMIT     sweep sd-924c13: a branch holds every limiting claim against what it holds
R-C4KEY       sweep sd-924c13: claim dated inside its key's window, verify.go ruleKeyWindow
R-C4SEAL      sweep sd-924c13: sealed once verified, adapter/sequencer
R-C5PERSIST   sweep sd-924c13: closure durable before the merge, adapter/sequencer
R-C6MERGE     sweep sd-924c13: branch-table chain to the initial table, adapter/sequencer
R-C6REQUEST   sweep sd-924c13: a request becomes its limiting claim in the same merge
R-C6SIGN      sweep sd-924c13: Sequencer claims name its own contributor, adapter/sequencer

# Deletion rules — planned and requested, and the gaps they explain.
R-DREQUEST    sweep sd-924c13: contribution/delete naming its target, contribution.go
R-DGAP        sweep sd-924c13: verification passes over an explained gap, verify.go
R-DEXPIRY     sweep sd-924c13: the key's closed window, verify.go verifyKeyWindow

# Field syntax.
R-FIELDS      sweep sd-924c13: field-name form and limit, field_taxonomy.go

# RQL — the query type and the native engine that is the conformance oracle.
R-QEVAL       sweep sd-924c13: fixed evaluation order, query.go
R-QSCOPE      sweep sd-924c13: branch defines the graph read, query.go
R-QHEAD       sweep sd-924c13: head narrows to its closure, query.go
R-QANCHOR     sweep sd-924c13: claim anchors the frontier, query_walk.go
R-QSTEPS      sweep sd-924c13: a step's edge/node globs and hop bounds, query_walk.go
R-QFORM       sweep sd-924c13: original or materialized field values, query.go
R-QSORT       sweep sd-924c13: sort keys over a total order, query_default.go
R-QLIMIT      sweep sd-924c13: results and time bounds, query.go
R-QLAYER      sweep sd-924c13: layer pinning leaves the result set alone, query.go
R-QSTREAM     sweep sd-924c13: tagged elements in order, query_encode.go
R-QREPORT     sweep sd-924c13: the report as the final element, query_report.go

# Translation to Cypher — the neo4j backend's own chapter.
R-QCYPHER     sweep sd-924c13: the translation answers what the native engine does
R-QCCLAUSE    sweep sd-924c13: block-by-block clause mapping, adapter/storage/neo4j
R-QCSTEP      sweep sd-924c13: a step as a variable-length segment, adapter/storage/neo4j
R-QCSCOPE     sweep sd-924c13: the confined set equals the scope, adapter/storage/neo4j
